@startuml fig2_design
' Research design for this revision: what varies, what is held equal, what is
' measured, and how the runs are ordered. The second column is the substance of
' the parity claim, and names the dimensions the earlier version left open.
skinparam dpi 300
skinparam defaultFontName "Helvetica"
skinparam defaultFontSize 15
skinparam rectangleFontSize 14
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowFontSize 13
skinparam nodesep 10
skinparam ranksep 14

rectangle "**Independent variable**\n\nStack configuration, four levels\n\nVapor, 2 event loops\nSpring Boot, Tomcat 200 (default)\nSpring Boot, Tomcat 64\nSpring Boot, Java 21 virtual threads" as IV #FFF8E1

rectangle "**Held equal across configurations**\n\n1.5 CPU cores, 1024 MB per container\n20 database connections per service\nRedis cache, 30 s time to live\n72 identical histogram buckets\nSame row caps on every list endpoint\nSame warm-up, run in its own process\nOne configuration measured at a time" as CV #DCE9FB

rectangle "**Measured**\n\nTail latency, client and server\nThroughput and error rate\nResident set size, steady and peak\nJVM heap, used and committed\nGarbage collection pauses\nBusy threads, database queue and wait\nControl-plane probe latency" as DV #E8F5E9

rectangle "**Protocol**\n\n4 workloads x 4 configurations\nx 5 repetitions = 80 sequential runs\n\nRepetitions interleaved, configuration\norder rotated, containers recreated and\ntables truncated before every run\n\nMedian, interquartile range, bootstrap\ninterval, Mann-Whitney U with A12" as PR #F5F5F5

IV -right-> CV
CV -right-> DV
DV -right-> PR

@enduml
